        },
        {
          "tag": "content",
          "role": "",
          "text": "",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "role": "",
              "text": "Before we discuss, there's something that needs to be said, because no one is saying it.",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "a",
                  "role": "",
                  "text": "Rewrite Bun in Rust",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/pull/30412"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "role": "",
              "text": "Bun stands where it does today because of Zig.",
              "attrs": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "role": "",
              "text": "",
              "attrs": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "figure",
              "role": "",
              "text": "",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "img",
                  "role": "",
                  "text": "",
                  "attrs": {
                    "src": "https://fs.liujiacai.net/cdn-img/zigcc/bun-rust-port.webp"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "role": "",
              "text": "",
              "attrs": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "role": "",
              "text": "Jarred chose Zig back then not because it was \"cool,\" but because Zig enabled a small team to rapidly prototype a high-performance JS runtime without a GC, without a heavy runtime. Zig's low friction,",
              "attrs": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "role": "",
              "text": "Jarred himself said: the architecture doesn't change, the data structures don't change.",
              "attrs": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "role": "",
              "text": "In plain English:Building the foundation with Zig, shipping the product with Zig, raising funding with Zig, and then switching to a more \"mainstream\" tech stack after the company gets acquired and has",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "strong",
                  "role": "",
                  "text": "the skeleton that the Rust rewrite inherits was built with Zig.",
                  "attrs": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "role": "",
              "text": "The Zig community doesn't need Bun's gratitude, but please don't pretend this rewrite happened because Zig itself is inadequate.",
              "attrs": {}
            },
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "role": "",
              "text": "",
              "attrs": {
                "id": "outline-container-headline-1",
                "class": "outline-2"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "h2",
                  "role": "",
                  "text": "The Real Issue No One Dares to Say",
                  "attrs": {
                    "id": "headline-1"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "tag": "div",
                  "role": "",
                  "text": "",
                  "attrs": {
                    "id": "outline-text-headline-1",
                    "class": "outline-text-2"
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "Now, let's discussitself.",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "a",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "the rewrite",
                          "attrs": {
                            "href": "https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/pull/30412"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "6,755 commits, branch name, PR opened May 8th, merged May 14th.",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "code",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "claude/phase-a-port",
                          "attrs": {
                            "class": "verbatim"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "Six days. A full rewrite of a production-grade JS runtime, merged in six days.",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "Let that number sit in your mind for a second.",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "There's a fundamental principle in software engineering:Not because it necessarily has bugs, but because when it does bug out, you won't know where to start looking. This principle isn't conservatism ",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "strong",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "code you don't understand should not run in production.",
                          "attrs": {}
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "6,755 commits, not a single line written by a human. The PR's reviewer list:reviewed it,reviewed it, and the only human reviewer alii's status was \"Awaiting requested review\" – hadn't even looked.",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "code",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "coderabbitai[bot]",
                          "attrs": {
                            "class": "verbatim"
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "tag": "code",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "claude[bot]",
                          "attrs": {
                            "class": "verbatim"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "Code written by Claude, reviewed by Claude. This closed loop isn't logically impossible, but it means:",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "strong",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "no human being has actually read this codebase in its entirety.",
                          "attrs": {}
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "role": "",
              "text": "",
              "attrs": {
                "id": "outline-container-headline-2",
                "class": "outline-2"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "h2",
                  "role": "",
                  "text": "\"All Tests Pass\" Doesn't Mean What You Think",
                  "attrs": {
                    "id": "headline-2"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "tag": "div",
                  "role": "",
                  "text": "",
                  "attrs": {
                    "id": "outline-text-headline-2",
                    "class": "outline-text-2"
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "Someone will push back here: the test suite passes on all platforms – isn't that validation?",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "No.",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "A test suite validatesIt does not validate:",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "strong",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "the correctness of known behavior on known paths.",
                          "attrs": {}
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "ul",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "li",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "Whether error paths are handled correctly",
                          "attrs": {}
                        },
                        {
                          "tag": "li",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "Behavior at boundary conditions under stress",
                          "attrs": {}
                        },
                        {
                          "tag": "li",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "State consistency in concurrent scenarios",
                          "attrs": {}
                        },
                        {
                          "tag": "li",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "Whether the memory model conforms to intent under extreme conditions",
                          "attrs": {}
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "Jarred himself admitted: memory issues when re-entering across JS boundaries – the Rust compiler can't handle that; it still relies on humans.",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "And those parts that rely on humans? No human has reviewed them.",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "The more fundamental issue is: AI translates code via– it ensures each function behaves identically to the original in isolation, but it doesn't understand thebetween functions – those design constrai",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "strong",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "local semantic equivalence",
                          "attrs": {}
                        },
                        {
                          "tag": "strong",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "global invariants",
                          "attrs": {}
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "This isn't a knock on Claude. This is a problem any translation tool – including human programmers – faces without thorough review. At the scale of 6,755 commits, this risk is amplified 6,755 times.",
                      "attrs": {}
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "role": "",
              "text": "",
              "attrs": {
                "id": "outline-container-headline-3",
                "class": "outline-2"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "h2",
                  "role": "",
                  "text": "After the Acquisition, the Risk Bearer Has Changed",
                  "attrs": {
                    "id": "headline-3"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "tag": "div",
                  "role": "",
                  "text": "",
                  "attrs": {
                    "id": "outline-text-headline-3",
                    "class": "outline-text-2"
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "There's a political-economy dimension here that technical discussions usually ignore.",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "In the early days, Bun was Jarred betting on himself. Using Zig then, iterating fast, accepting tech debt – that was reasonable startup logic with self-assumed risk.",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "Now Bun has been acquired by a major company, and its user base consists of real production systems. The risk bearer of this rewrite is no longer Jarred, but every engineer running Bun in production a",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "Jarred says this version is still in canary, and there's optimization and cleanup work to do before official release.",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "Canary is a line of defense, but it's not human review. Optimization and cleanup are code quality concerns, not comprehension concerns.",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "strong",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "A codebase that no one on the team has fully read – no matter how comprehensive the tests, no matter how long canary runs – its internal state is a black box to its maintainers.",
                          "attrs": {}
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "This will become very real pain at some future severe bug's debugging scene.",
                      "attrs": {}
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "role": "",
              "text": "",
              "attrs": {
                "id": "outline-container-headline-4",
                "class": "outline-2"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "h2",
                  "role": "",
                  "text": "Zig's \"Problems\" Were Misdiagnosed",
                  "attrs": {
                    "id": "headline-4"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "tag": "div",
                  "role": "",
                  "text": "",
                  "attrs": {
                    "id": "outline-text-headline-4",
                    "class": "outline-text-2"
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "Let's return to Jarred's stated reasons for migration: the Zig codebase had too many use-after-free bugs, double-frees, and memory leaks on error paths.",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "This is true. But the conclusion that \"Zig doesn't work\" drawn from this diagnosis is wrong.",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "The correct diagnosis is:This isn't a bug in Zig – it's a structural mismatch between Zig's design goals and Bun's business model.",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "strong",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "in a commercial project that prioritizes rapid iteration, the cognitive tax of manual memory management exceeded the team's budget.",
                          "attrs": {}
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "Zig's target users are: systems programmers who know what they're doing and are willing to pay the price for ultimate control. TigerBeetle used Zig to write a database with virtually no memory bugs, b",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "Bun's team culture is fast iteration, fast shipping, fast bug fixes. There's a fundamental tension between this and the rigorous memory discipline that Zig demands. This is a mismatch between Bun and ",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "Interpreting \"our team frequently makes mistakes with this tool\" as \"this tool is inadequate\" is an attribution error. The hammer doesn't fit, but it's not the hammer's fault.",
                      "attrs": {}
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "role": "",
              "text": "",
              "attrs": {
                "id": "outline-container-headline-5",
                "class": "outline-2"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "h2",
                  "role": "",
                  "text": "So, Will This Rewrite Work?",
                  "attrs": {
                    "id": "headline-5"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "tag": "div",
                  "role": "",
                  "text": "",
                  "attrs": {
                    "id": "outline-text-headline-5",
                    "class": "outline-text-2"
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "Honestly:",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "strong",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "short-term it'll probably be fine; long-term there are structural risks.",
                          "attrs": {}
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "Short-term: tests cover the main paths, the canary phase will expose obvious issues, and Rust's compiler guarantees eliminate an entire class of memory bugs. On the surface, everything looks normal.",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "Long-term: this codebase has 6,755 commits that no human has fully read. When a bizarre concurrency bug appears six months from now, when some boundary condition triggers anomalous behavior under a sp",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "The difference between these two becomes crystal clear at 3 AM during a production incident.",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "strong",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "A system no one has understood doesn't mean it has no bugs – it means when bugs appear, no one knows why.",
                          "attrs": {}
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "This is the real technical bet of this rewrite: not Zig vs Rust, but",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "strong",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "whether AI-generated, unreviewed code can be maintained long-term in production environments.",
                          "attrs": {}
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "This question is far more complex than \"all tests pass,\" and far more profound than \"Rust memory safety.\"",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "The answer – we'll wait and see.",
                      "attrs": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "em",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "Zig built the foundation, Claude erected the building, human reviewers are still en route.",
                          "attrs": {}
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "p",
                      "role": "",
                      "text": "",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "em",
                          "role": "",
                          "text": "How long this building remains habitable depends on whether anyone can read the blueprints the first time it springs a leak.",
                          "attrs": {}
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "role": "",
              "text": "",
              "attrs": {
                "id": "outline-container-headline-6",
                "class": "outline-2"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "h2",
                  "role": "",
                  "text": "References",
                  "attrs": {
                    "id": "headline-6"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "tag": "div",
                  "role": "",
